"A cowboy's accoutrements consist of the fol-
lowing articles (the articles and prices are first
class and are possessed by a first-class man):

Crematory,
}
Crematorium,}
A place to burn the dead.

Fruechschoppen, In the vocabulary of the Hei-
delberg students, the beer drank before noon;
the early pint.

Mannishness, The quality of being like a man;
usually applied to a woman who displays
masculine characteristics.

Saratoga-chips, Thin slices of potatoes, fried;
prepared first by Moon of Saratoga lake, and
now in general use.

Second-class, Next in grade below the highest;
also a general name for designating inferior
quality.
